  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "> In the",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> authentication process the same select statement gets executed several",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> times (see the full SQL log here:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://fedora.fiz-karlsruhe.de/docs/Wiki.jsp?page=Sql)"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://fedora.fiz-karlsruhe.de/docs/Wiki.jsp?page=Sql)",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "text": " :",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": ">",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> SELECT path FROM objectPaths WHERE token='changeme:27'",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> SELECT path FROM objectPaths WHERE token='changeme:27'",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> SELECT path FROM objectPaths WHERE token='changeme:27'",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> SELECT path FROM objectPaths WHERE token='changeme:27'",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> SELECT path FROM objectPaths WHERE token='changeme:27'",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> SELECT path FROM objectPaths WHERE token='changeme:27'",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> SELECT path FROM objectPaths WHERE token='changeme:27'",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> SELECT path FROM objectPaths WHERE token='changeme:27'",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> SELECT path FROM objectPaths WHERE token='changeme:27'",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": ">",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> I guess these selects could be reduced to one statement. The statement",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> is not terribly expensive and will even be optimized/cached by most",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> database systems but nonetheless it can hurt performance since the",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> column doesn't have an index.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
