  "description": "<p>&gt; In the<br/>\n&gt; authentication process the same select statement gets executed several<br/>\n&gt; times (see the full SQL log here:<br/>\n&gt; <a href=\"http://fedora.fiz-karlsruhe.de/docs/Wiki.jsp?page=Sql\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://fedora.fiz-karlsruhe.de/docs/Wiki.jsp?page=Sql</a>) :<br/>\n&gt;<br/>\n&gt; SELECT path FROM objectPaths WHERE token='changeme:27'<br/>\n&gt; SELECT path FROM objectPaths WHERE token='changeme:27'<br/>\n&gt; SELECT path FROM objectPaths WHERE token='changeme:27'<br/>\n&gt; SELECT path FROM objectPaths WHERE token='changeme:27'<br/>\n&gt; SELECT path FROM objectPaths WHERE token='changeme:27'<br/>\n&gt; SELECT path FROM objectPaths WHERE token='changeme:27'<br/>\n&gt; SELECT path FROM objectPaths WHERE token='changeme:27'<br/>\n&gt; SELECT path FROM objectPaths WHERE token='changeme:27'<br/>\n&gt; SELECT path FROM objectPaths WHERE token='changeme:27'<br/>\n&gt;<br/>\n&gt; I guess these selects could be reduced to one statement. The statement<br/>\n&gt; is not terribly expensive and will even be optimized/cached by most<br/>\n&gt; database systems but nonetheless it can hurt performance since the<br/>\n&gt; column doesn't have an index.</p>",
